WEBVTT

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.200
Can you... hear...

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.010
...my voice?

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.410
Hey...

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.560
<i>Orion?</i>

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:44.420
What's wrong?

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:49.280
<i>Orion, I can't hear you very well.</i>

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.300
Hey.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.510
What's wrong?

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:55.480
N-Nothing.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.330
Let's go home.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.520
Thanks for bringing me home...

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.620
I'm going home now.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.410
What?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.380
Oh...

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.020
Why are you making that face?

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.260
What am I to you?

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.320
An old friend? Someone like family?

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.310
Or have you acknowledged me as your boyfriend?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.300
I made you acknowledge me as your boyfriend once before,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.900
so I thought we understood each other.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.900
But with how you've been acting, I'm not so sure anymore.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.320
While we're dealing with this,

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.510
I definitely don't want to go back to being like family again.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.540
We finally started dating,

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.710
and we built up a relationship.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:06.420
I know it's not your fault that you lost your memories, but...

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.340
I know that, but...

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:12.950
I can't.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.060
<i>The fact that my memories haven't returned...</i>

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.990
<i>...is hurting Shin.</i>

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.970
In any case, it was my fault.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.190
I'm sorry.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:45.960
Forgive me.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.470
<i>I wonder why he can't tell me about the accident.</i>

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.740
<i>Is there a reason why he can't say?</i>

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.740
Oh?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.050
Your bandages are already off.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.140
Your neck must be cooler.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.380
Yeah. I'm sorry if I worried you.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:09.320
Visually, it's a bit of a shame.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.040
I thought it might bring in some new core customers.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.450
Morning!

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.660
Mr. Manager, take a look at this!

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.070
A fireworks show?

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:26.510
I thought it'd be nice to go with everyone,

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.580
but I don't think she's ready for big crowds yet.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.420
So why don't we have our own fireworks show here in town?

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:33.760
Oh my!

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.430
That's a great idea.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.230
I love it!

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.640
I'll text Toma and Mine.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:42.600
Should we invite Shin too?

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.950
Would he be busy studying for exams?

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.120
I'm calling him now.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.800
He picked up.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.580
Here.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.810
Sawa? What is it?

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:55.880
Um...

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.070
Huh? Why are you...

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:03.490
It turns out we're going to light some fireworks tonight,

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.080
so I was wondering if you'd like to come.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.550
I have prep school today.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:12.840
I can't.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.030
Really?

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.460
I told you.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.820
I'm studying for exams.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.760
Yeah. That's right.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:22.930
Is he coming?

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:23.760
No.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.680
Really? That's unusual.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.490
He turned down a direct invitation from you?

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.690
Toma and Mine said they're both coming.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:32.530
What about Shin?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.440
He said he couldn't come.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.700
I see.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.230
Well, that's how it goes.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.150
Well then, let's put this discussion aside for now.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:44.300
It's time to open.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.870
Go greet the guests.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.990
Let's start with the rockets!

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.590
Hey, Sawa.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.970
Why are we starting with the rockets?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.700
Shouldn't we save those for the end?

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:13.400
What? Let's start with a blast!

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:18.150
Maybe we can set up some handheld fireworks around the rockets!

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.870
That's dangerous.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.450
That's strange.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:26.090
I thought my coworkers invited me to a fireworks show...

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.620
I feel like it's turned into a babysitting gig.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:28.960
I wanna light some rockets!

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.140
I wonder why.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.250
I wanna light some rockets!

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.280
Hey, Sawa, wait!

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.500
All right, let's do it.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.750
Have fun, but be careful with the fire.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.460
Hey, Sawa, Mine, calm down.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.310
Toma, do something about this.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.310
Mine, let's light some rockets!

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.190
Waka...

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:48.870
Let me see that. I'll light it for you.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.910
Sawa, relax.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.270
Shin.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.580
Should I not have come?

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.000
It's not that...

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.140
Come with me for a second.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:17.230
Shin?

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:23.310
About the accident...

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.450
You really don't remember?

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:27.640
No.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.840
Think of this as the Shinano forest and listen to me.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:40.400
You might remember something.

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:45.120
We were able to be alone that night, like we are now.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:48.530
I confronted you about sharing a room with Sawa.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.080
"Why are you in the same room as Sawa?

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:53.940
I'll leave my room, so you come out too."

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.710
Then you said,

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.960
"I didn't come on this trip to do that.

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.670
We're all here together."

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:04.960
You don't remember?

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:06.690
Nothing at all?

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:12.080
You said, "Why do you always say things like that?

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:15.850
You must enjoy embarrassing me."

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:17.310
I don't enjoy it.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.450
I'm seriously inviting you.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.490
Do you really think of me as your boyfriend?

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.680
You still only see this as a vacation?

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.070
I'm always ready to bite down.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:30.850
I'm going back now.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:31.810
Wait.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:32.830
Don't!

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:38.210
You don't have to be afraid.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:42.460
I haven't done anything to scare you.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:48.370
You ran off,

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.070
like you did now,

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:52.850
and fell from the cliff.

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:54.620
You were hurt.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:00.400
And it was all my fault.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:05.060
For some reason, I felt like I needed to rush things.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.550
I blocked your escape,

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.970
hoping you'd acknowledge me as your boyfriend right then.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.110
I was greedy.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.890
Yesterday was the same.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:19.400
It took so long before it felt like we were really going out,

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:23.810
and just when I thought we had moved past being just friends,

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:26.090
this happened.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:27.410
Shin...

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:31.800
I'm sorry. This isn't really the time to be thinking about this.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:37.390
I know you're going through a lot more than I am right now.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:42.810
I should be the one protecting you this time.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.290
I feel so pathetic.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:51.490
Even though you supported me when I was about to break...

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:53.110
You...

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.720
saved me.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:01.210
I did?

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:03.600
You don't remember that either.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:24.950
Want to try it too?

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.100
Sparklers in a secluded place?

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.110
I suppose it's very like you.

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:36.790
It's pretty, isn't it?

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:40.470
I don't really see the fun in it...

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:44.830
But you've always liked this kind of thing, haven't you?

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:49.940
I don't mind seeing you enjoy something small like this.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:58.100
Before, you said that I saved you.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:03.230
If it's too difficult to talk about, you don't have to.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:08.610
But I thought I should ask you for our future's sake.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:11.360
That's true.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:17.360
My father...

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:20.890
killed...

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:24.720
He... killed a man.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:28.660
Did you...

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.830
remember something?

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:32.690
No...

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:34.380
<i>It was wrong.</i>

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:38.390
<i>It wasn't about Shin.</i>

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:43.520
A drunk picked a fight with my father,

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:45.990
and my father pushed him away.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:50.400
But something else hit one of his vital points, and he died.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:56.400
Of course, he thinks he did a terrible thing to him and to his family.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.960
I was only a kid at the time,

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:04.090
so I didn't understand why people were calling my father a murderer.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:09.820
From then on, people looked at me differently.

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:12.880
Even my close friends

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:17.170
distanced themselves from me and feared me.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:21.090
But despite all that, you and Toma didn't change.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:23.940
If you two hadn't been there for me,

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:26.610
I don't think I'd've been able to reconnect with anyone ever again.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.110
Beautiful!

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:35.460
I'm grateful to you.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:40.210
But that was because you tried.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:41.730
I wasn't trying.

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:44.520
I had given up and was just going with the flow.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.440
But now I'm trying.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:51.750
All right. Here comes the next one!

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:56.750
To be honest, there were times when Toma really got on my nerves.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:05.700
It was you who showed me that surrendering to misfortune and giving up was just running away.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:07.160
So,

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.790
I won't give up anymore...

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:14.140
On you either.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:19.690
Shin.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:24.910
Thank you for telling me about the accident.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:28.910
Hey!

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.590
Hey!

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.760
Join us!

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:33.920
Let's go...

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:36.200
to our slightly annoying brother's side.

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:41.090
Hey, it went over there!

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:43.280
What did?

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:45.010
The spinner.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:56.400
Shin! I thought I was gonna die!

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:58.350
You're exaggerating.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.690
You dodged it well enough.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:04.870
<i>I'm glad I heard the story.</i>

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.170
It's been so long since we all lit fireworks together.

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:16.210
It feels like we've really gone back to being kids.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:16.900
Yeah.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.260
Still, Toma, your reaction was over the top.

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:22.170
Surprise attacks are surprising, man.

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.320
It was really high up.
<i>I had fun.</i>

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:27.160
I didn't expect your counterattack.
<i>I want to treasure these memories.</i>

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.560
<i>I don't want to lose them.</i>

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:33.600
<i>But why can't I remember anything?</i>

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.160
<i>Will the memories I lost...</i>

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:39.250
<i>never return?</i>

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.190
<i>Or...</i>

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:44.950
Do you remember this place?

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:51.420
We used to play here a lot when we were kids.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:52.160
Here?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:57.030
We used to call it "crayfish park" or something.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:58.290
That's right.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.920
There were a lot of crayfish here at one time, so we started calling it that.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:07.170
Now that I think about it, someone must've released those crayfish into the lake.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:10.060
We got so wrapped up in catching them...

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:14.940
And our parents got mad and told us to "put them back in the lake!"

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:18.730
I bet they were just scared of them.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.130
You said it.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:26.780
And I'd like to give those nostalgic memories back to her, little by little.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.870
That's an awfully nice thing for you to say, Shin.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:35.360
Not really.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.880
Did Toma think he was being considerate?

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.910
I'll get out of your way now.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.800
I'll leave the rest in your hands.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:55.670
I'm sure you're tired. Want to go home?

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:57.740
Yeah.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.190
But maybe in a little while.

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:07.530
I'm always saying terrible things

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:09.960
and being so forceful,

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.480
but I'll always protect you.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:17.750
I decided I'd never hurt you again.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.670
Shin...

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.500
Thank you.

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:31.760
Since I lost my memories and didn't know what to do,

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.360
I was so unsure...

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:39.170
And you told me out of the blue that we were dating,

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:41.350
but I had no idea.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:45.440
The truth is, I couldn't believe it.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:47.300
I bet.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:48.780
No.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:52.830
Now, well...

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.920
Now I'm relieved.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:00.580
Don't push yourself.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:07.550
It took some time before too for you to go out with me once I confessed to you.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:15.310
I'll ask you once again.

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.200
Go out with me.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:21.270
I don't want to go back to being friends anymore.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:25.320
Go out with me.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:29.200
I'll make you forget about the distance between us right away.

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:34.180
Shin... But I still don't know you...

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:35.990
very...

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:38.370
That's fine.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:45.750
Actually, that was the same answer you gave me the first time I asked you out.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:02.600
Don't be so forceful.

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:07.320
I'll show you that I'm a man, starting now.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.560
You'll never know when I'm going to kiss you.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.080
So stay on your toes, idiot.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.390
That's harsh.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:21.600
Wanna go?

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.610
Yeah. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:27.180
Yeah.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:39.170
<i>I want to get back the memories that I lost.</i>

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.650
<i>For my sake.</i>

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.130
<i>For Shin's sake.</i>

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.380
<i>I wished on a falling star...</i>

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:08.250
What? I...

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:16.560
Ikki?

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:18.680
Um...

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:21.970
You finally picked up. It's me.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.600
We both have today off from work, right?

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:28.100
Can you go out? Let's go somewhere.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.970
Where do you want to go? We have time today.

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:33.070
Um...

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:34.280
I'll be at your house

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.450
in thirty minutes.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:38.550
Um...

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.210
This is...

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.810
I know I wrote something here.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.270
What's going on?

00:19:58.190 --> 00:19:59.020
Hello?

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:00.520
Hey, are you all right?

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:04.800
It seemed like you weren't feeling well before.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.330
So I was concerned.

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:07.980
Sorry.

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:10.550
I just woke up, so...

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:12.860
Really? That's fine.

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:14.930
I'll be there in about ten minutes.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:17.190
I understand.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.770
See you soon.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:20.160
Okay...

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:24.000
In any case, I have to get ready.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.170
What could've happened with Ikki all of a sudden?

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:43.600
<i>Those girls...</i>

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.030
I have to go now.

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:53.190
No!

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:55.480
Ikki, don't say that.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:57.570
I told you, I can't today.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.860
I already have plans.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.110
I really can't.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.700
What? No way.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:05.950
Sorry.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:09.690
Is something wrong?

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:11.300
You're not jealous, are you?

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:13.300
What? I...

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:15.880
I guess once in a blue moon...

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:20.030
Well, personally, I enjoy it.

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:21.010
It's more stimulating.

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:25.390
To make up for it, I'll answer one request from you.

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:29.240
Personally, I'd love a sexual request.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.430
What do you want me to do?

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:36.940
<i>Why is Ikki?</i>

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:39.280
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:40.130
<i>Is this...</i>

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:42.410
<i>How can...</i>

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:44.990
Hey,

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.520
do you mind?

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:49.620
Rika...

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:27.360
Fireworks are really nice!

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:30.130
The big ones that explode in the night sky are great,

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:32.620
but the small ones that pop in little sparks in your hand,

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.090
the sparklers, are sort of bittersweet too!

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:39.200
Good kids shouldn't mimic throwing spinner fireworks, though!
